   "body": "Seen 3 more times on 2026-11-06, each time on a diff that touches no MP code, a 60 s `.timeLimit(.minutes(1))` hit while the simulator was slow (neighbouring `PollModelTests` / `TopicSearchModelTests` cases took 60–100 s):\n- #505 job 127768763466: `switchingSegmentDuringASearchStopsIt`\n- #506 job 127772213039: `aCancelledSearchDoesNotUndoWhatWasReadMeanwhile`\n- #495 job 127805467134 (docs-only): `switchingSegmentDuringASearchStopsIt`\n\nBoth tests carry `.timeLimit(.minutes(1))` (MessageListSplitTests.swift:131, :156); the limit, not a hang, is the likely trigger, but that is not proven. Jobs re-run once. Raising `priority`: it now reds unrelated PRs. Not fixed now (cloud lots frozen, #368).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
